# Fixture: lists_reordered.ttl
#
# Purpose: the SAME triples as lists.ttl except the unionOf list elements are
# in a different order (Dog, Fish, Cat instead of Cat, Dog, Fish). The list
# pass treats order as semantically significant — different order must produce
# a DIFFERENT canonical form (distinct urn:owlcompare:list:<hash>).

@prefix : <http://example.org/lists#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<http://example.org/lists> a owl:Ontology .

:Pet a owl:Class ;
    owl:equivalentClass [
        a owl:Class ;
        owl:unionOf ( :Dog :Fish :Cat )
    ] .

:Cat a owl:Class .
:Dog a owl:Class .
:Fish a owl:Class .
